msgstr "I am"

msgid "I come"
msgstr "I come"

msgid "I do, I make"
msgstr "I do, I make"

msgid "I drink"
msgstr "I drink"

msgid "I eat"
msgstr "I eat"

msgid "I go"
msgstr "I go"

msgid "I learn, I study"
msgstr "I learn, I study"

msgid "I listen"
msgstr "I listen"

msgid "I live"
msgstr "I live"

msgid "I look, I watch"
msgstr "I look, I watch"

msgid "I love"
msgstr "I love"

msgid "I read"
msgstr "I read"

msgid "I see"
msgstr "I see"

msgid "I sit"
msgstr "I sit"

msgid "I speak"
msgstr "I speak"

msgid "I wait"
msgstr "I wait"

msgid "I want"
msgstr "I want"

msgid "I want to read."
msgstr "I want to read."

msgid "I work"
msgstr "I work"

msgid "In class"
msgstr "In class"

msgid "In lesson {commands} you learned <0/> as a whole word. It comes from the <1>-da</1> infinitive, with <2>-ge</2> in place of its ending: <3/> gives <4/>, and <5/> gives <6/>"
msgstr "In lesson {commands} you learned <0/> as a whole word. It comes from the <1>-da</1> infinitive, with <2>-ge</2> in place of its ending: <3/> gives <4/>, and <5/> gives <6/>"

msgid "In lesson {present} you learned a verb as two forms: <0/>, to read, and its present, <1/>. A dictionary gives a third between them, the <2>-da</2> infinitive: <3/>."
msgstr "In lesson {present} you learned a verb as two forms: <0/>, to read, and its present, <1/>. A dictionary gives a third between them, the <2>-da</2> infinitive: <3/>."

msgid "It can have a stem of its own: <0>loe-n</0>, <1>räägi-n</1>, <2>õpi-n</2>. The <3>-da</3> infinitive keeps the <4>-ma</4> infinitive’s stem."
msgstr "It can have a stem of its own: <0>loe-n</0>, <1>räägi-n</1>, <2>õpi-n</2>. The <3>-da</3> infinitive keeps the <4>-ma</4> infinitive’s stem."

msgid "Its -da infinitive is {da}, its present {n}."
msgstr "Its -da infinitive is {da}, its present {n}."

msgid "its <0>-da</0> infinitive"
msgstr "its <0>-da</0> infinitive"

msgid "Learn a verb as three forms, the <0>-ma</0> infinitive, the <1>-da</1> infinitive and the present: <2>lugema, lugeda, loen</2>."
msgstr "Learn a verb as three forms, the <0>-ma</0> infinitive, the <1>-da</1> infinitive and the present: <2>lugema, lugeda, loen</2>."

msgid "Learn every Estonian verb as three forms: <0>lugema, lugeda, loen</0>. Most verbs make the middle one by swapping <1>-ma</1> for <2>-da</2>; some take <3>-ta</3>, and a few take <4>-la</4>, <5>-na</5> or a bare <6>-a</6>."
msgstr "Learn every Estonian verb as three forms: <0>lugema, lugeda, loen</0>. Most verbs make the middle one by swapping <1>-ma</1> for <2>-da</2>; some take <3>-ta</3>, and a few take <4>-la</4>, <5>-na</5> or a bare <6>-a</6>."

msgid "Lessons {negation} and {commands} called <0/> the <1>ma</1> form, after <2>ma loen</2>. From here on it is the present, and the <3>-ma</3> infinitive is <4/>."
msgstr "Lessons {negation} and {commands} called <0/> the <1>ma</1> form, after <2>ma loen</2>. From here on it is the present, and the <3>-ma</3> infinitive is <4/>."

msgid "Listening only, no microphone"
msgstr "Listening only, no microphone"

msgid "Make the <0>-da</0> infinitive"
msgstr "Make the <0>-da</0> infinitive"

msgid "Mari teaches a class. When she tells them what to do, the verb builds on the <0>-da</0> infinitive; when she says what the class does, on the present. Fill each gap."
msgstr "Mari teaches a class. When she tells them what to do, the verb builds on the <0>-da</0> infinitive; when she says what the class does, on the present. Fill each gap."

msgid "Most verbs keep the stem"
msgstr "Most verbs keep the stem"

msgid "Most verbs make the <0>-da</0> infinitive by swapping <1>-ma</1> for <2>-da</2>: <3/>, <4/>. Whatever sits before <5>-ma</5> usually stays as it is."
msgstr "Most verbs make the <0>-da</0> infinitive by swapping <1>-ma</1> for <2>-da</2>: <3/>, <4/>. Whatever sits before <5>-ma</5> usually stays as it is."

msgid "Most verbs swap <0>-ma</0> for <1>-da</1> on the same stem: <2>elama, elada</2>. The <3>-da</3> infinitive keeps that stem when the present changes it: <4>lugeda, loen</4>."
msgstr "Most verbs swap <0>-ma</0> for <1>-da</1> on the same stem: <2>elama, elada</2>. The <3>-da</3> infinitive keeps that stem when the present changes it: <4>lugeda, loen</4>."

msgid "Nearly. Play the ones you missed once more."
msgstr "Nearly. Play the ones you missed once more."

msgid "One of the verbs that take <0>-ta</0>: <1>{ma}</1>, <2>{da}</2>."
msgstr "One of the verbs that take <0>-ta</0>: <1>{ma}</1>, <2>{da}</2>."

msgid "Only the ending changes: <0>luge-ma</0>, <1>luge-da</1>."
msgstr "Only the ending changes: <0>luge-ma</0>, <1>luge-da</1>."

msgid "Play all three"
msgstr "Play all three"

msgid "Play the <0>-ta</0>, <1>-la</1>, <2>-na</2> and <3>-a</3> forms above once more, then try again."
msgstr "Play the <0>-ta</0>, <1>-la</1>, <2>-na</2> and <3>-a</3> forms above once more, then try again."

msgid "Play the forms above once more, then try again."
msgstr "Play the forms above once more, then try again."

msgid "Present"
msgstr "Present"

msgid "Read. To more than one, or polite."
msgstr "Read. To more than one, or polite."

msgid "See a verb’s <0>-ma</0> infinitive and type its <1>-da</1> infinitive, then hear it. The keys under the field type õ, ä, ö, ü, š and ž."
msgstr "See a verb’s <0>-ma</0> infinitive and type its <1>-da</1> infinitive, then hear it. The keys under the field type õ, ä, ö, ü, š and ž."

msgid "Sit down. To more than one, or polite."
msgstr "Sit down. To more than one, or polite."

msgid "Some take <0>-ta</0>: <1>oodata</1>. <2>Olema</2>, <3>tulema</3> and <4>minema</4> take <5>-la</5> or <6>-na</6>: <7>olla, tulla, minna</7>."
msgstr "Some take <0>-ta</0>: <1>oodata</1>. <2>Olema</2>, <3>tulema</3> and <4>minema</4> take <5>-la</5> or <6>-na</6>: <7>olla, tulla, minna</7>."

msgid "Some verbs take <0>-ta</0>: <1/>, <2/>; <3/>, <4/>; <5/>, <6/>. <7>Ootama</7> and <8>vaatama</8> also turn the t of their stem into d: <9>oota-</9>, <10>ooda-</10>. Lesson {gradation} explains that change; for now, learn these three whole."
msgstr "Some verbs take <0>-ta</0>: <1/>, <2/>; <3/>, <4/>; <5/>, <6/>. <7>Ootama</7> and <8>vaatama</8> also turn the t of their stem into d: <9>oota-</9>, <10>ooda-</10>. Lesson {gradation} explains that change; for now, learn these three whole."

msgid "Speak. To more than one, or polite."
msgstr "Speak. To more than one, or polite."

msgid "Swap <0>-ma</0> for <1>-da</1>: <2>{ma}</2>, <3>{da}</3>."
msgstr "Swap <0>-ma</0> for <1>-da</1>: <2>{ma}</2>, <3>{da}</3>."

msgid "Tahan, I want, is followed by the -da infinitive."
msgstr "Tahan, I want, is followed by the -da infinitive."

msgid "Tap a form"
msgstr "Tap a form"

msgid "That holds even when the present changes the stem: <0/> gives <1/>, though I read is <2/>. The same goes for <3/> and <4/>. Switch between the forms and tap a line to hear it."
msgstr "That holds even when the present changes the stem: <0/> gives <1/>, though I read is <2/>. The same goes for <3/> and <4/>. Switch between the forms and tap a line to hear it."

msgid "The -da infinitive of {ma}."
msgstr "The -da infinitive of {ma}."

msgid "The <0>-ma</0> infinitive"
msgstr "The <0>-ma</0> infinitive"

msgid "The form a dictionary lists first. Take off <0>-ma</0> and you have its stem, <1>luge-</1>."
msgstr "The form a dictionary lists first. Take off <0>-ma</0> and you have its stem, <1>luge-</1>."

msgid "The other persons build on the present; for most verbs, the command to more than one builds on the <0>-da</0> infinitive: <1>te loete, lugege!</1>"
msgstr "The other persons build on the present; for most verbs, the command to more than one builds on the <0>-da</0> infinitive: <1>te loete, lugege!</1>"

msgid "The present"
msgstr "The present"

msgid "The present is <0>joon</0>. Drop <1>-ma</1>, turn <2>oo</2> into <3>uu</3> and add <4>-a</4>."
msgstr "The present is <0>joon</0>. Drop <1>-ma</1>, turn <2>oo</2> into <3>uu</3> and add <4>-a</4>."

msgid "The present is <0>lähen</0>, with a stem of its own. Drop <1>-ema</1> and add <2>-na</2>."
msgstr "The present is <0>lähen</0>, with a stem of its own. Drop <1>-ema</1> and add <2>-na</2>."

msgid "The present is <0>näen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1>, turn g into h and add <2>-a</2>."
msgstr "The present is <0>näen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1>, turn g into h and add <2>-a</2>."

msgid "The present is <0>olen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1> and add <2>-la</2>."
msgstr "The present is <0>olen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1> and add <2>-la</2>."

msgid "The present is <0>söön</0>. Drop <1>-ma</1>, turn <2>öö</2> into <3>üü</3> and add <4>-a</4>."
msgstr "The present is <0>söön</0>. Drop <1>-ma</1>, turn <2>öö</2> into <3>üü</3> and add <4>-a</4>."

msgid "The present is <0>teen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1>, turn g into h and add <2>-a</2>."
msgstr "The present is <0>teen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1>, turn g into h and add <2>-a</2>."

msgid "The present is <0>tulen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1> and add <2>-la</2>."
msgstr "The present is <0>tulen</0>. Drop <1>-ema</1> and add <2>-la</2>."

msgid "The present of {ma}."
msgstr "The present of {ma}."

msgid "The same stem with <0>-da</0>"
msgstr "The same stem with <0>-da</0>"

msgid "These four short verbs end their <0>-da</0> infinitive in a bare <1>-a</1>, and the stem changes too. <2/>, to do, and <3/>, to see, turn g into h: <4/>, <5/>."
msgstr "These four short verbs end their <0>-da</0> infinitive in a bare <1>-a</1>, and the stem changes too. <2/>, to do, and <3/>, to see, turn g into h: <4/>, <5/>."

